--- a/docs/ci-evidence.md
+++ b/docs/ci-evidence.md
@@ -37,3 +37,12 @@ The reader makes authenticated GET requests only to `api.github.com`, with the e
 Jobs are read from that run's exact attempt endpoint. Every returned job must belong to the same run and attempt; exactly one `ci-required` must be completed and successful. A final filtered run-list readback rejects a newer matching run, changed attempt or changed success state during job inspection. Each collection must be complete: counts, page lengths, next-page indicators and distinct IDs are checked with a maximum of five 100-record pages per list read. Missing, changing, malformed, denied or truncated evidence fails closed. The whole read has a 30-second deadline, and API responses have a four MiB size limit. API response URLs and pagination URLs never determine request destinations.
 
 Success writes only an allowlisted JSON receipt to the step summary: source SHA, numeric repository/workflow/run/attempt/job IDs, fixed workflow path, and completed/success enums. Failure writes a fixed error code without raw API data, URLs, exception text, headers or credentials. Offline Node tests cover trust identity, newer failure/pending results, exact attempt jobs, missing/duplicate aggregates, pagination, malformed/API/timeout failures, safe output and the actual workflow mode condition. These fixtures do not establish a live GitHub CI result or authorize a release.
+
+## Reusing a validated tree on master
+
+A merged PR or a fast-forwarded `deliver/` branch has usually just passed the same gates on the same files. The `master` push run therefore looks for that result first and skips the product jobs when it finds it. The run, its `ci-required` job and its `push`/`master`/exact-SHA identity still exist, so the CD prerequisite above is unchanged.
+
+- **Recording.** `record-validated-tree` runs after `ci-required` succeeds, only when the scope mode is `full` and the `verify` job validated the whole acceptance map (`META_PARENT` unset or `pure-chore`; a numeric parent only validates that parent's entries). Only `workflow_dispatch` runs and same-repository `pull_request` runs record. It uploads a small artifact named `ci-validated-tree-<tree SHA>`, where the tree is that of the checked-out merge result or branch tip. The job is `continue-on-error`, so a recording failure cannot fail the CI run.
+- **Lookup.** On a `master` push, `scripts/find-validated-tree.py` lists unexpired artifacts with that exact name. A hit counts only if its run is this repository's own `ci.yml`, was a `pull_request` or `workflow_dispatch` run from this repository (not a fork), and completed with `success`. Any API failure, malformed response or miss means no reuse and the full gates run.
+- **Result.** A hit makes scope mode `reused`: product scope with every product job skipped. `scripts/check-ci-required.py` accepts `reused` only when no job was expected, so it cannot mask a skipped gate in another mode.
+- **When it does not apply.** The tree differs (for example `master` advanced before the merge, so the merge result differs from the tested one), the earlier run was selective or used a numeric parent, the artifact expired after 14 days, or the lookup failed. Those pushes run every gate as before.
